# Zenodo API token for scripts/publish_zenodo.py
#
# Copy this file to `.zenodo_token` and replace the placeholder line at the
# bottom with your token. Lines starting with # are ignored, so these notes can
# stay in the file.
#
# Get a token at:
#     https://zenodo.org/account/settings/applications/tokens/new/
#
# Scopes needed:
#     deposit:write      create a deposit and upload files into it
#     deposit:actions    publish it (this is what mints the DOI)
#
# Zenodo shows the token exactly once, at creation time. If you lose it, make a
# new one rather than hunting for it.
#
# `.zenodo_token` is gitignored and must stay that way — a leaked token can
# rewrite or delete the lab's deposits. Keep it readable only by you:
#     chmod 600 .zenodo_token
#
# For a dry run against https://sandbox.zenodo.org — a separate site, with its
# own separate account and token — put that token in `.zenodo_token.sandbox`
# and pass --sandbox. Recommended before a 9 GB upload to the real thing.

PASTE_YOUR_ZENODO_TOKEN_HERE
